{%- comment -%}
  main-collection — the collection listing page.

  Ported 31/08/2026 from the old theme's 56.8KB T4S section. Visual target:
  design-system treatment with live's structure kept — the two-column
  rail + grid, the toolbar above the grid, the bespoke tile in the grid, the
  promo card under the filters. Sizing, type, spacing and colour follow
  fye-core.css; none of live's own values were carried across.

  THE FILTERS ARE NOT OURS. Live renders an empty
  <div id="cloud_search_filters_sidebar"> and the xCloud app injects the entire
  filter rail into it at runtime. The old section's native Shopify facet button
  was hidden with inline CSS on every non-editor request, and `type_filters`
  is "facets_tags", so no theme-rendered facet form has been on this page for
  some time. This port keeps the mount point, styles what the app drops into
  it, and does NOT rebuild a facet form. If xCloud is ever removed, the filter
  UI has to be designed, not recovered.

  xCLOUD HAS TWO INJECTION POINTS, and only one of them is wanted:
    #cloud_search_filters_sidebar  the rail. We place this one, in the aside.
    #cloud_search_filters_root     a horizontal chip bar plus a "Filter" link,
                                   injected by the app on its own initiative,
                                   outside our markup. Hidden — see the
                                   stylesheet. Live suppresses it too.

  THE MOUNT POINT IS NOT ENOUGH ON ITS OWN. xCloud arrives as an APP EMBED,
  stored in config/settings_data.json, which Shopify auto-generates. A newly
  created theme has no app embeds enabled, so the div renders and stays empty
  with no error anywhere. If the filters are missing, check the theme editor's
  App embeds panel BEFORE looking at this file.

  FILTER ICONS — three families, two mechanisms, all of them live's:
    metal + profile   inline SVG from snippets/fye-filter-icons, cloned into
                      the app's rows by fye-ui.js. Live did this with an
                      inline <script> in a custom-liquid block.
    stone shape       CSS mask-image on ::before, from Shopify Files
                      (icon101–icon110, baguette.svg). Store-level Files, not
                      theme assets, so the URLs resolve unchanged here.
    stone type        CSS background colour on ::before. Tokens in core.
  The last two need no JS at all and are pure CSS, exactly as on live
  (assets/custom.css). Only metal and profile need cloning, because a metal
  swatch is a layered gradient rather than a single fill.

  Deliberately NOT ported, and why:
    · product_des 1–9 (nine tile designs)  — one card, snippets/product-card
    · layout_des grid/masonry              — masonry was never enabled
    · list/grid view switch, items-per-row switcher — the markup was commented
      out in live already; the `layout` block now renders the result count,
      which is all it actually did
    · load-more / infinite scroll          — live is on "default" pagination
    · countdowns, vendors, colour + size swatches, quick view, compare,
      the isotope and ajax stacks — none enabled on this store
    · image_ratio / image_size / image_position — the card is square, sitewide
  34 of the old section's settings are gone. Setting IDs that remain are
  unchanged, so templates/collection.json needs no edit.

  Block types ("layout", "filter", "sortby") keep their old names because the
  JSON template references them.

  Sorting is a real <select> that fye-ui.js submits on change (data-fye-sort).
  It must navigate rather than GET-submit a form: xCloud keeps its active
  filters in the query string, and a bare form would drop every one of them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign cols = s.col_dk | default: '4'
  assign cols_mb = s.col_mb | default: '2'
  assign per_page = s.limit | default: 24

  comment
    A `select` setting is a STRING, and Liquid refuses to compare a string to
    an integer — it raises rather than coercing, and the whole tag renders as
    an error. `cols` stays a string for the CSS custom property; `cols_n` is
    the number the eager/lazy test below needs.
  endcomment
  assign cols_n = cols | plus: 0

  assign has_sort = false
  assign has_count = false
  assign has_filter = false
  for block in section.blocks
    case block.type
      when 'sortby'
        assign has_sort = true
      when 'layout'
        assign has_count = true
      when 'filter'
        assign has_filter = true
    endcase
  endfor

  assign sort_current = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by

  assign show_promo = false
  if s.fye_promo_heading != blank
    assign show_promo = true
  endif
  assign promo_link = s.fye_promo_link | default: '/pages/contact-us'
  assign tile_link = s.fye_tile_link | default: '/pages/create-your-own-ring'
-%}

{%- paginate collection.products by per_page -%}
{%- liquid
  assign first_index = paginate.current_offset | plus: 1
  assign last_index = paginate.current_offset | plus: paginate.page_size
  if last_index > collection.products_count
    assign last_index = collection.products_count
  endif

  comment
    The bespoke tile only earns a slot on page one, and only when there are
    enough products that it reads as part of the grid rather than as the grid.
  endcomment
  assign tile_on = false
  if s.fye_tile_heading != blank and paginate.current_page == 1 and collection.products.size >= 4
    assign tile_on = true
  endif
  assign tile_at = s.fye_tile_position | default: 4
-%}
<section class="band band--white coll" data-screen-label="Collection">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="coll__layout">

      <aside class="coll__rail">
        <details class="coll__railbox" open>
          <summary class="coll__railtoggle">
            {%- if has_filter -%}
              {{ s.fye_rail_title | default: 'Refine' }}
            {%- else -%}
              Refine
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- render 'icon', name: 'chevron-down', class: 'icon--sm coll__railchev' -%}
          </summary>

          <div class="coll__railbody">
            {%- if s.fye_rail_head -%}
              <div class="coll__railhead">
                <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.fye_rail_title | default: 'Refine' }}</p>
                <a class="coll__clear" href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ s.fye_rail_clear | default: 'Clear all' }}</a>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              xCloud's rail mount point. Empty on purpose — the app fills it.
              The id is load-bearing and must not be renamed or wrapped in a
              way that changes it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div id="cloud_search_filters_sidebar"></div>

            {%- comment -%}
              The metal and profile icon library. Inert markup: a <template>
              plus two gradient defs. Rendered here rather than in theme.liquid
              so a page without a filter rail does not carry it.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- render 'fye-filter-icons' -%}

            {%- if show_promo -%}
              <div class="coll__promo">
                <p class="coll__promotitle">{{ s.fye_promo_heading }}</p>
                {%- if s.fye_promo_body != blank -%}
                  <p class="coll__promobody">{{ s.fye_promo_body }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if s.fye_promo_label != blank -%}
                  <a class="link coll__promolink" href="{{ promo_link }}">{{ s.fye_promo_label }}</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      </aside>

      <div class="coll__main">

        {%- if has_count or has_sort -%}
          <div class="coll__bar">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- case block.type -%}
                {%- when 'layout' -%}
                  <p class="coll__count" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    {%- if collection.products_count > 0 -%}
                      Showing {{ first_index }}–{{ last_index }} of {{ collection.products_count }} results
                    {%- else -%}
                      Showing 0 results
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </p>

                {%- when 'sortby' -%}
                  <div class="coll__sort" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <label class="visually-hidden" for="coll-sort">Sort by</label>
                    <select id="coll-sort" class="coll__select" data-fye-sort>
                      {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                        <option value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value == sort_current %} selected{% endif %}>{{ option.name }}</option>
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </select>
                  </div>
              {%- endcase -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if collection.products.size > 0 -%}
          <ul class="pgrid coll__grid" style="--pcols: {{ cols }}; --pcols-mb: {{ cols_mb }};">
            {%- for product in collection.products -%}
              {%- if tile_on and forloop.index == tile_at -%}
                <li class="coll__tile">
                  <div class="coll__tileinner">
                    <div class="coll__tilewords">
                      {%- if s.fye_tile_eyebrow != blank -%}
                        <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.fye_tile_eyebrow }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <p class="coll__tiletitle">{{ s.fye_tile_heading }}</p>
                      {%- if s.fye_tile_body != blank -%}
                        <p class="coll__tilebody">{{ s.fye_tile_body }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                    {%- if s.fye_tile_label != blank -%}
                      <a class="link coll__tilelink" href="{{ tile_link }}">{{ s.fye_tile_label }}</a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
              <li>
                {%- if forloop.index <= cols_n -%}
                  {%- render 'product-card', product: product, loading: 'eager' -%}
                {%- else -%}
                  {%- render 'product-card', product: product, loading: 'lazy' -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- else -%}
          <p class="coll__empty lead">No products match these filters. <a href="{{ collection.url }}">Clear all filters</a> to see everything in this collection.</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
          <nav class="coll__pages" aria-label="Pagination">
            <p class="coll__pageof fine">Page {{ paginate.current_page }} of {{ paginate.pages }}</p>
            <ul class="coll__pagelist">
              {%- if paginate.previous.is_link -%}
                <li><a class="coll__page" href="{{ paginate.previous.url }}" rel="prev">Previous</a></li>
              {%- endif -%}
              {%- for part in paginate.parts -%}
                {%- if part.is_link -%}
                  <li><a class="coll__page" href="{{ part.url }}">{{ part.title }}</a></li>
                {%- elsif part.title == '&hellip;' -%}
                  <li><span class="coll__gap">…</span></li>
                {%- else -%}
                  <li><span class="coll__page is-current" aria-current="page">{{ part.title }}</span></li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if paginate.next.is_link -%}
                <li><a class="coll__page" href="{{ paginate.next.url }}" rel="next">Next</a></li>
              {%- endif -%}
            </ul>
          </nav>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if s.show_desc and collection.description != blank -%}
      <div class="coll__desc prose">{{ collection.description }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>
{%- endpaginate -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ============================================================================
   THE xCLOUD FILTER RAIL
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Everything in this block styles markup we do not own and cannot add classes
   to, so the selectors name xCloud's classes. That is a deliberate departure
   from conventions.md, and it is the only way to skin an app-rendered rail.
   Written scoped and unscoped where the app injects outside .fye, the same
   reason .visually-hidden is written twice in core.

   Live carried all of this with !important on nearly every declaration
   (assets/custom.css). None of it is repeated here: if the app ever raises its
   own specificity the rail loses our skin and keeps working, which is the safe
   failure. If a rule silently stops applying, that is why.
   ========================================================================== */

/* The app's horizontal chip bar, injected above the page content on its own
   initiative: a "Filter" link plus a row of filter-name chips. We only want
   the rail. Live suppresses it too. Hiding it costs nothing on mobile — the
   rail's own <details> summary is the filter trigger there. */
.cloud-search-page-controls,
.fye .cloud-search-page-controls {
  display: none;
}

/* --- the row ------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Whole-row rollover rather than a hover on the label alone: the row is the
   target, and a 5px/8px inset gives the ground something to be. */
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  width: 100%;
  padding: 5px 8px;
  transition: background var(--dur) var(--ease), color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:hover {
  background: var(--filter-row-hover);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:has(input:checked) {
  background: var(--filter-row-checked);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value input[type='checkbox'] {
  accent-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:focus-within .cloud-search-filter-value__name {
  color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name {
  color: var(--teal);
}

/* xCloud caps each filter group and scrolls it internally. With icons in the
   rows that puts a scrollbar through the middle of the swatches. */
.fye .cloud-search-filter__values {
  max-height: none;
  overflow: visible;
}

/* --- stone shapes: mask-image on ::before --------------------------------
   The silhouettes are Shopify FILES, not theme assets — store-level uploads,
   so these URLs resolve on any theme without copying anything. A mask rather
   than an <img> so one colour declaration drives resting, hover and checked
   across all eleven. */

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Round Brilliant'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Oval'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Cushion'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pear'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald Cut'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Radiant'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Princess'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Marquise'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Asscher'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Heart'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Baguette'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  content: '';
  display: inline-block;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: 26.4px;
  height: 26.4px;
  margin-right: 9px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  background-color: var(--gem-shape);
  mask-position: center;
  mask-size: contain;
  mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  -webkit-mask-position: center;
  -webkit-mask-size: contain;
  -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  transition: background-color var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Round Brilliant'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon101.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon101.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Oval'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon102.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon102.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Cushion'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon103.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon103.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pear'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon104.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon104.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald Cut'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon105.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon105.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Radiant'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon106.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon106.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Princess'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon107.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon107.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Marquise'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon108.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon108.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Asscher'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon109.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon109.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Heart'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon110.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/icon110.svg);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Baguette'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/baguette.svg);
  -webkit-mask-image: url(/cdn/shop/files/baguette.svg);
}

/* --- stone colours: a 20px dot on ::before -------------------------------
   The inset hairline is not decoration: Diamond is #FFFFFF and Opal is
   near-white, and without it those two rows have no visible swatch at all. */

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Diamond'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Black Diamond'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Sapphire'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Ruby'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Aquamarine'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Tanzanite'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Opal'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Fire Opal'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Morganite'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Amethyst'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Blue Topaz'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Citrine'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Garnet'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Peridot'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pink Tourmaline'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  content: '';
  display: inline-block;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: 20px;
  height: 20px;
  margin-right: 9px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  border-radius: 50%;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge);
  transition: box-shadow var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Diamond'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-diamond); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Black Diamond'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-black-diamond); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Sapphire'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-sapphire); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Ruby'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-ruby); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-emerald); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Aquamarine'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-aquamarine); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Tanzanite'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-tanzanite); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Opal'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-opal); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Fire Opal'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-fire-opal); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Morganite'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-morganite); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Amethyst'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-amethyst); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Blue Topaz'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-blue-topaz); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Citrine'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-citrine); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Garnet'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-garnet); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Peridot'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-peridot); }
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pink Tourmaline'] .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before { background: var(--gem-pink-tourmaline); }

/* Selected and hover states for both ::before families. A dot cannot change
   colour to show selection — it IS a colour — so it gains a teal ring, while
   the shape silhouettes recolour like any other icon. */

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  background-color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  background-color: var(--teal);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Diamond']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Black Diamond']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Sapphire']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Ruby']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Aquamarine']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Tanzanite']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Opal']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Fire Opal']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Morganite']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Amethyst']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Blue Topaz']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Citrine']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Garnet']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Peridot']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pink Tourmaline']:hover .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  background-color: inherit;
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Diamond']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Black Diamond']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Sapphire']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Ruby']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Emerald']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Aquamarine']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Tanzanite']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Opal']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Fire Opal']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Morganite']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Amethyst']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Blue Topaz']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Citrine']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Garnet']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Peridot']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value[data-filter-value='Pink Tourmaline']:has(input:checked) .cloud-search-filter-value__name::before {
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gem-edge), 0 0 0 2px var(--teal);
}

/* --- metal and profile icons, cloned in by fye-ui.js ---------------------
   Colour sits on the wrapper and reaches the SVG through currentColor, so
   hover and checked are one declaration each rather than one per icon. */

.fye .fic-defs {
  position: absolute;
  width: 0;
  height: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.fye .fic-wrap {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  margin-right: var(--s2);
}

.fye .fic {
  display: block;
}

.fye .fic--metal {
  width: 26px;
  height: 26px;
  color: var(--metal-edge);
}

.fye .fic--profile {
  width: 46px;
  height: 27px;
  color: var(--metal-edge-profile);
}

.fye .fic__lbl {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 10.5px;
  font-weight: var(--fw-semi);
  fill: var(--metal-label);
  text-anchor: middle;
  dominant-baseline: middle;
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:hover .fic,
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:focus-within .fic {
  color: var(--sage);
}

.fye .cloud-search-filter-value:has(input:checked) .fic {
  color: var(--teal);
}

/* ============================================================================
   THE LISTING ITSELF
   ========================================================================== */

/* This section always follows the collection masthead, which collapses this
   band's top padding via a :has() rule in fye-collection-intro. --sect-y is
   still reduced here for the case where the masthead is absent. Sets the
   token, never a padding declaration. */
.fye .coll {
  --sect-y: var(--s8);

  /* THE ROW HEIGHT, DECLARED ONCE.
     The rail head and the toolbar are one row across two columns; their
     hairlines only line up if both boxes resolve to the same height.

     Do NOT do this by asserting `min-height: 44px` on both. That was the first
     attempt and it was 22px out, because box-sizing is border-box: on the rail
     head, min-height INCLUDES the 20px padding, so the box was 44px total; the
     toolbar meanwhile grew past its min-height because the <select> renders
     45px intrinsically, giving 45 + 20 + 1 = 66px. Two boxes both claiming
     "44px", nowhere near each other.

     So: one variable sets the row's content height, the select is pinned to it
     rather than left to its intrinsic size, and the rail head asks for that
     height PLUS its own padding. */
  --coll-row: 44px;
}

.fye .coll__layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 260px minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--s10);
  align-items: start;
}

/* --- rail ---------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* The rail is one component at every width: a <details> that is forced open
   above 900px with its summary hidden, and a real disclosure below it. Two
   copies of the filter markup would give xCloud two mount points with the
   same id, which is why this is not a show/hide pair. */
.fye .coll__railbox {
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .coll__railtoggle {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s3);
  min-height: 56px;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-button);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  cursor: pointer;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .coll__railtoggle::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}

.fye .coll__railchev {
  transition: transform var(--dur) var(--ease);
}

.fye .coll__railbox[open] .coll__railchev {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}

.fye .coll__railbody {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s6);
  padding-bottom: var(--s6);
}

/* Pairs with .coll__bar. Height: --coll-row + --s5 padding, stated as a calc
   because border-box would otherwise eat the padding out of the row. Clearance
   below: --s4 margin + the --s6 railbody gap = --s8, matching the bar. */
.fye .coll__railhead {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s4);
  min-height: calc(var(--coll-row) + var(--s5));
  padding-bottom: var(--s5);
  margin-bottom: var(--s4);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .coll__clear {
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* --- promo card ---------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .coll__promo {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
  padding: var(--s6);
  background: var(--mist);
}

.fye .coll__promotitle {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h4);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.fye .coll__promobody {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .coll__promolink {
  align-self: flex-start;
}

/* --- toolbar ------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* Pairs with .coll__railhead. No min-height: the row's height comes from the
   select, which is pinned to --coll-row below. */
.fye .coll__bar {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s5);
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  padding-bottom: var(--s5);
  margin-bottom: var(--s8);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .coll__count {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* `height`, not `min-height` — an intrinsically-45px control is what threw the
   two columns out of line. */
.fye .coll__select {
  width: auto;
  min-width: 220px;
  height: var(--coll-row);
  min-height: 0;
  padding-block: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

/* --- the bespoke tile ---------------------------------------------------- */

/* Sits in a grid cell alongside the cards, so it inherits the square media
   ratio rather than setting a height. */
.fye .coll__tile {
  display: flex;
}

.fye .coll__tileinner {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--s6);
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  padding: var(--s7);
  background: var(--ivory);
}

.fye .coll__tilewords {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--s3);
}

.fye .coll__tiletitle {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-h2);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.fye .coll__tilebody {
  margin: 0;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

.fye .coll__tilelink {
  align-self: flex-start;
}

/* --- empty state --------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .coll__empty {
  margin: 0;
  padding-block: var(--s10);
}

/* --- pagination ---------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .coll__pages {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s4);
  margin-top: var(--s10);
  padding-top: var(--s8);
  border-top: var(--hairline);
}

.fye .coll__pageof {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .coll__pagelist {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: var(--s2);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.fye .coll__pagelist > li {
  margin: 0;
}

.fye .coll__page {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-width: var(--coll-row);
  min-height: var(--coll-row);
  padding-inline: var(--s3);
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
}

.fye .coll__page.is-current {
  border-color: var(--line-strong);
}

.fye .coll__gap {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: var(--coll-row);
  padding-inline: var(--s2);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
}

/* --- description --------------------------------------------------------- */

.fye .coll__desc {
  margin-top: var(--s10);
}

/* --- breakpoints. Media queries LAST, always. ---------------------------- */

@media (min-width: 901px) {
  /* Above the collapse the rail is not a disclosure at all: the summary goes,
     and the body is forced visible whatever the element's open state, so a
     visitor who collapsed it on a phone does not find a desktop page with no
     filters. */
  .fye .coll__railbox {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .fye .coll__railtoggle {
    display: none;
  }

  .fye .coll__railbody {
    display: flex;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .fye .coll__layout {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s7);
  }

  /* Stacked, there is no second column to line up with, and the summary is
     already labelled "Refine" — so the head would repeat it. */
  .fye .coll__railhead {
    display: none;
  }

  .fye .coll__bar {
    margin-bottom: var(--s7);
  }
}

@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .coll__bar {
    align-items: stretch;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s3);
  }

  .fye .coll__select {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .fye .coll__tileinner {
    aspect-ratio: auto;
    padding: var(--s6);
  }
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   TOUCH TARGETS — 02/09/2026, from the first collection smoke run.
   "Clear all" measured 48×21 and "Ask an expert" 129×24. Both are controls in
   their own right rather than words in a sentence, so both take the 44px
   minimum. inline-flex keeps them on their existing baseline; the extra
   height is padding, so nothing around them moves.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .coll__clear,
.fye .coll__promolink {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 44px;
}

/* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE FILTER APP'S ROWS — 02/09/2026. Not our markup: cloud-search renders
   these. Each row is a <label> wrapping a 16px checkbox and the value name, so
   the label carries the 44px minimum and the whole row becomes the target. The
   checkbox is left alone at 16px.

   FRAGILE BY NATURE: if the app renames its classes, this stops applying
   silently. It can only ever add height, so it cannot break the page — but
   re-run fyeSmoke on a collection page after any cloud-search update.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .cloud-search-filter-value {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 44px;
}
{% endstylesheet %}

